{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather to Me seventy men from the elders of Israel</b> — Our Rabbis have already mentioned that there are seventy nations corresponding to the seventy languages, and each and every one has a constellation in the heavens and a prince above, as it is said concerning Daniel (Daniel 10:13): \"and the prince of the kingdom of Persia,\" and it is written (ibid.) alongside the kings of Persia, and likewise \"and behold, the prince of Greece is coming\" (ibid. v. 20). And this is what is said (Isaiah 24:21): \"HaShem will punish the host of the height in the height\" (Mekhilta de-Shirata 2). And they said (Sukkah 55a) that the water-libation of the Festival alludes to them, and in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer (ch. 24) the Holy One, blessed be He, said to the seventy angels who surround the throne of His glory: \"Come, let Us confound their language.\" Therefore the number of those who went down to Egypt was seventy, and He commanded this number for the judges of Israel, for this number comprehends all opinions, inasmuch as it comprehends all powers and nothing is lacking from them. And likewise at the giving of the Torah: \"and seventy of the elders of Israel\" (Exodus 24:1), for it is fitting that upon this complete number the glory of the Shekhinah should rest, just as it is in the upper camp, for Israel are the hosts of HaShem on earth — just as the Ark and the Mercy-Seat and the Tabernacle were made in the likeness of those who minister on high, and the standards were made in similitude of the Chariot that Ezekiel saw, in order to rest the Shekhinah upon them on earth just as the Shekhinah is in heaven. Behold, Moses upon the seventy elders is an allusion to Israel that they are one nation on earth. And our Rabbis received (Sanhedrin 2a) that every Great Sanhedrin that sits in the House of HaShem in the place that He shall choose to cause His name to dwell there — thus their number shall be seventy, and the prince over them like Moses our Teacher, and behold they are seventy-one. And likewise the letters of the great explicit Name are seventy-two, corresponding to the princes, and the unique Name which is the singular Master over all of them. And to this the verse alludes in saying: \"Elohim stands in the congregation of El; in the midst of Elohim He judges\" (Psalms 82:1), for the Shekhinah is with them to give assent through them. And Scripture says: \"How long will you judge unjustly?\" (ibid. v. 2), warning them — since the honored Name is with them in the matter of judgment, how do you not fear Him to pervert judgment, in the sense of \"the people who provoke Me to My face\" (Isaiah 65:3). And He says further (Psalms 82:6): \"I said, you are Elohim, and all of you sons of the Most High,\" for your number is like the number of the princes on high and the singular Master, and I said that you shall sit the seat of Elohim on earth. \"Nevertheless, as a man you shall die,\" as the first man who was banished from his honored place and died — so shall you be banished from the House of HaShem and die, and as one of the princes on high you were, and you shall fall from that station. And I have already mentioned this matter in the section of \"And these are the judgments\" (Exodus 21:6)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:32.709319513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}